(\hat{i}-m \hat{j}) \cdot(\hat{j}+\hat{k}) & =|\hat{i}-m \hat{j}| \cdot|\hat{j}+\hat{k}| \cdot \cos \left(\frac{\pi}{3}\right) \\
-m & =\left|\sqrt{1+m^2}\right| \cdot\left|\sqrt{1^2+1^2}\right| \cdot \frac{1}{2} \\
\text{ or, } -\sqrt{2} m & =\sqrt{1+m^2}
\end{aligned}$
Squaring both sides, we get
$\begin{aligned}
2 m^2 & =1+m^2 \Rightarrow m^2=1 \\
m & = \pm 1
\end{aligned}$

